      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm trying to decide how to elevate these. \n\nWhen you mention that Kenji or Andre \"fit well\" in crime dramas, is that because those characters naturally lend themselves to that kind of conflict, or is it more about the audience's expectations for those specific backgrounds? Like, if I moved Kenji into a high-society role, would it feel out of place or just \"unrealistic\" to a typical viewer? I'm trying to figure out if I'm fighting against natural storytelling instincts or just hitting clichés.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
