      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The reason Kenji and Andre seem to fit well in crime dramas is a mix of both natural character traits and audience tropes that we're used to seeing. Marcus might be seen as street-smart, but the hooded look alone is a little common. With Kenji, his quiet intensity and tech savviness are definitely qualities that audiences might expect to see in a young, tech-focused character in a crime drama. If you want to create top-tier characters for your pilot, the better route might be to avoid these tropes at all costs and focus on unique characters and scripts that don't come off as trying too hard to be \"original.\" A high-society drama doesn't readily welcome someone like Kenji—a stereotypical nerd who might clash with the world of the ultra-privileged. It could feel out of place and not conform to the typical expectations of a \"new-money\" character. It's more about keeping in mind the natural storytelling instinct and what stories are and have been told to audiences before.",
